WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.060
<i>It's the second round of the Regionals.</i>

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:06.980
<i>My name's Shigeno Daigo, and I was put 
into the starting lineup as catcher.</i>

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.610
<i>However, I put us in trouble because of
my inexperience and got subbed out.</i>

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>With no outs and runners on first and second,</i>

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.450
<i>our regular catcher, Andy, stepped up.</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.730
Nice one, Andy!

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.780
Yeah! A double play!

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.170
Nice!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.030
<i>They got us.</i>

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.090
<i>I didn't expect him to have the 
courage to waste a pitch there.</i>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.590
<i>Wow!</i>

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:38.350
<i>So that's a real catcher?</i>

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.810
Two outs!

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.430
Hmph, not bad.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.790
Nijigaoka

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.790
Mifune

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.620
<i>The score is two–nothing.</i>

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.550
All-Out Battle

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.550
<i>The Nijigaoka Beetles have 
the lead going into the sixth.</i>

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.800
<i>Two outs, and a runner on second.</i>

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.550
Two down, two down!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.520
Nijigaoka Beetles

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.520
Pitcher   Tamaki

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.730
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.230
Nijigaoka Beetles

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.230
Manager   Komori

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.230
<i>From no outs with runners on first and 
second to two outs with a runner on second.</i>

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.710
<i>Their pitcher's been rejuvenated 
since this catcher came on the field.</i>

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.230
Catcher

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.230
Suzuki Andy

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.490
Mifune Dolphins

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.490
Coach   Fujii

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.490
Mifune Dolphins

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.490
Manager   Tashiro

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.660
<i>First base is open.</i>

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.490
<i>Don't get into a battle of wills
with their cleanup.</i>

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.610
<i>Walk him.</i>

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.490
Pitcher

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.490
Urabe Hayato

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:08.720
Huh?

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.130
They're walking him, huh?

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.790
Well, it's understandable.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:19.980
Time out!

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:24.510
What's up? You don't want to walk this guy?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.930
How did you know?

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.270
Of course I knew.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.390
How many years have I been 
catching your pitches?

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.490
What's this?

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.650
Don't tell me they actually 
want to take this guy on...

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.030
What?!

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.100
Play!

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.250
They're not going to walk him?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.750
Nice. I like your style.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.040
Hey! Shouldn't you stop them, Tashiro?

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.820
Maybe I should,

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.510
but I've given Andy the final say 
when it comes to judgment calls.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:04.030
This battery must have some kind of plan.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.890
Wanting to take him on 
isn't an ego thing.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.360
If the score was 0-0, 
or we were in the lead,

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.400
I'd walk him without a second thought.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:20.910
Foul!

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.630
<i>But right now, we're two runs behind.</i>

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.450
<i>We've only got two more chances to attack.</i>

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.890
<i>Up to now, this ace who plays cleanup</i>

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:33.290
<i>hasn't given up a hit, 
let alone a chance to score.</i>

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.670
<i>In order to get our team into 
the counterattacking mindset,</i>

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.250
<i>we need to crush our opponent's ace.</i>

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.340
Strike two!

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:49.510
<i>And if we shut them out this inning after 
the chances they've had, they'll be deflated.</i>

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.680
<i>It'll reverse the flow of the game.</i>

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.440
<i>I'll shut him down here</i>

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.870
<i>and give us the momentum!</i>

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.860
<i>Got him!</i>

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.150
Right field!

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.660
Right fielder

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.660
Sakura Mutsuko

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.190
Center, center!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.750
Go home!

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.880
What are you doing, Mutsuko-chan?!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.830
No!

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.210
But why?

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.920
Third run!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.020
Yeah! Good job, Tamaki!

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.140
Sweet! A double!

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.020
That moron. We had it in the bag.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.390
What the hell was she playing at?!

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.960
What happened, Mutsuko-chan?

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.060
You were right underneath the ball.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.150
I heard someone shout "center."

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:48.030
Center

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:48.030
Satou Hikaru

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.060
I thought that meant you were coming for it.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:51.280
Katsumata-kun, did you shout "center"?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.330
No, I didn't.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:56.880
That girl fell for his fake-out.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.180
Fake-out?

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.790
The bench and the umpire 
were too far away to hear it,

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:06.010
but the person who tricked her
 by calling "center"...

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.580
was the runner who just batted.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.300
Is such a cheap trick even legal?

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.210
I don't like it,

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.820
but it's a simple error
that wouldn't have happened

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:19.020
if she'd realized it wasn't 
a teammate shouting.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.020
<i>Damn it. Tamaki used that trick again.</i>

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.110
<i>I left it up to the battery, 
but in the end, it all went wrong.</i>

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.070
<i>That extra run at this stage 
of the game has really hurt us.</i>

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.330
Nagai

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.330
Kishimoto

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.330
Well, look at that. I told you so.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.440
That's what happens when you put 
a complete beginner out on the field.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.300
Nijigaoka

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.300
Mifune

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:50.950
Play!

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.530
<i>Snap out of it, Urabe.</i>

00:06:56.530 --> 00:07:00.350
<i>That last run was a real punch 
to the gut, but it's not over yet!</i>

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:04.020
<i>Why are you throwing 
such a halfhearted pitch?!</i>

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.190
Sweet! It got through!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.380
What?!

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.660
Out!

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.790
We only gave up one run.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.620
What the hell were you doing out there?!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.890
How could you miss such an easy fly?!

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.380
I pushed for you to start because
I believed in your abilities,

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:41.640
and you repay me by wrecking this game 
for us by doing everything half-assed?!

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.830
I-It wasn't like that!

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.700
I went for it, but then, 
someone yelled "center"...

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.270
Cool it, Urabe!

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.990
Stop making excuses!

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:55.610
Anyone can tell by just looking at you 
that you're not giving your best out there!

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:59.750
You're holding back cause you feel bad for
Nagai or something like that, aren't you?!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.000
Takahashi

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:04.000
If you take someone's spot,

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.070
it's <i>your</i> responsibility to play 
at least as well as they would have!

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:13.330
You owe it to the player whose spot 
you took to give it all you've got!

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.280
Shigeno and Satou are 
giving everything out there!

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.680
There's nothing worse than a talented player 
refusing to live up to their potential!

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:26.160
That's enough, Urabe.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:26.770
Damn it!

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.940
I think the person who shouted 
"center" was on the other team.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.990
I'll go tell him they tricked you, 
and it wasn't because of a lack of effort.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.700
No. It's fine.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:42.250
Huh?

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.380
Bottom of the sixth.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.300
Dolphins at the plate.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.630
Batting eighth, second 
baseman, Katsumata-kun.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.300
Out.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.190
<i>That insurance run we got
has made all the difference.</i>

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:13.040
<i>If we hadn't scored when 
Tamaki was at the plate as cleanup,</i>

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.600
<i>our ace up there on the mound 
would be down in the dumps right now.</i>

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.980
One down, one down!

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:22.880
Batting ninth, right fielder,

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.200
Sakura-san.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:28.330
I <i>need </i>to win two more games
so we can play the Touto Boys!

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.300
And I can't do it without you guys helping me.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.480
Strike!

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.190
<i>I wasn't taking this seriously.</i>

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.230
<i>Please don't pick me.</i>

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.280
Batting ninth, right field, Sakura.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.640
I've... been benched?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.120
<i>Urabe-kun was right.</i>

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.180
<i>I was feeling guilty about 
what happened to Nagai-kun.</i>

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.220
Put Sakura into the starting 
lineup as an outfielder.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:12.250
I think she should be near the 
top of the batting order as well.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:17.380
<i>Urabe-kun really believed in my abilities
and stuck his neck out for me,</i>

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.760
<i>and yet, I completely 
disregarded his feelings.</i>

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:22.710
<i>No...</i>

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:29.050
<i>I disregarded everyone's feelings when 
they've all been trying so hard to win.</i>

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:33.730
<i>I...</i>

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.490
<i>I only cared about myself!</i>

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:41.740
She did it!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.450
Keep running, Mutsuko-chan!

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:49.080
She's fast!

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.830
I didn't realize she could run that fast!

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.910
All right! A triple!

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:59.220
She broke his no-hit, no-run game!

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.550
Nice batting, Sakura!

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.600
Batting first, shortstop, Kimura-kun.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.020
<i>That's right. This is where 
we start to fight back!</i>

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.300
Play.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:21.110
To think Sakura would be the first to 
hit that slow ball to the opposite side...

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:25.010
See? I told you she had skills.

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:29.910
<i>We're three runs behind. All we can do 
is hit and hope a chance comes our way.</i>

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.080
<i>We're three runs ahead.</i>

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:36.020
<i>You can let the runner on third score, 
but make sure you secure an out.</i>

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.710
Shortstop

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.710
Kimura

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:43.370
This is his third time up. 
He should have got his eye in by now.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:45.010
Not to mention...

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:49.850
<i>If the fielders drop their center of gravity 
during his windup, it's a fastball.</i>

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:51.270
<i>If they don't...</i>

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:52.770
<i>...it's a slow ball!</i>

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.280
Yeah!

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:56.270
All right!

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.320
It found the gap!

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.030
Awesome! We clawed back a run. 3-1!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.530
Great!

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.020
Kimura got a clean hit there.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:17.130
Yeah, at this stage, Daigo's way of telling 
which pitch is coming is really paying off!

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:20.630
Batting second, left fielder, Shigeno-kun.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.020
Play!

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:23.550
Keep us running, Shigeno!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.020
Nijigaoka

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.020
Mifune

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:43.350
<i>To be totally honest, they got that last run 
because my catching went to pot.</i>

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:46.620
Strike.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.690
Daigo-kun! You can do it!

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:49.990
<i>Two more runs.</i>

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:53.130
<i>If I keep us alive long enough for 
Hikaru to get to the plate again...</i>

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.400
<i>The best way to get myself on base is...</i>

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.170
<i>There!</i>

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>I have to aim at the least-defended place
during their Eephus shift!</i>

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:10.600
A push bunt!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:19.150
Safe!

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.360
All right!

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.570
Nice bunt!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.780
One out, runners on first and second!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.940
Damn it.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:30.040
<i>They've discovered the Eephus 
shift's biggest weak spot.</i>

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:35.490
Most people in that situation would have 
wanted to swing big, so well done, Daigo.

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:40.590
Yeah. It's also not easy to get a solid 
bunt like that from a ball that slow.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:46.760
Nah, Shigeno-kun's been practicing his 
bunts after reviewing the first-round game.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:49.870
I think he was confident he could do it.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.780
Well done!

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.910
Nice aim, Daigo!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:54.720
Huh?

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.050
Oh, fiddlesticks!

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:58.480
Oh, Gramps! Grandma!

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.080
You've been here watching?

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.980
It's no good hiding your face now.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.740
Why are you all the way over there?

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:11.910
Batting third, pitcher, Urabe-kun.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:15.160
<i>Watch the fielders and 
if it's a slow ball, run.</i>

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:19.680
<i>Their batters are gaining in confidence.</i>

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.460
<i>Have they figured out 
which pitch is coming?</i>

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:27.930
<i>No, if they had, the runner on first 
would've started running much earlier.</i>

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:33.640
Strike!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:39.100
All right! A perfect double steal!

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:40.650
Time out!

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:43.580
All right, one more hit and we're tied.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:49.320
So, Tashiro, why didn't you get Kimura 
to steal when Daigo was batting?

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.030
I didn't want the other team to realize

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:55.460
that we'd figured out their pitching 
pattern by stealing bases so easily.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:59.330
I was waiting for a real opportunity 
like this one to come along.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.040
Seriously?!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.960
Wow. You're like a real strategist.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:07.550
I bet they'll try something 
to counter us now.

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:08.500
What?

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.020
They know what type of pitch is coming?

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:15.930
Yeah, the runners are looking at the 
fielders to decide whether to steal or not.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:16.840
Huh?

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:20.890
You guys are setting yourselves 
for the fastball too early.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.970
Use your slow-ball stance 
until the very last moment.

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:26.020
Yes, sir!

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:30.280
And you two in the battery: our 
opponent's getting used to your slow balls.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.740
Use them as setup pitches,
and finish them off with fastballs.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:34.900
Yes, sir.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.600
Manager?

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.820
One hit and they're tied, and they have 
the meat of the order coming up.

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.080
Is this really enough?

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:46.880
What are you trying to say?

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:51.590
Can't I use the secret weapon?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:59.920
We're in a corner here. They're used 
to our slow balls and half-speed balls.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.600
If we don't do more, we risk losing.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.360
Please let me use the secret weapon!

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:18.490
One hit and we're tied.
 I'm counting on you, Urabe.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.260
Play.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.070
Ball.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.890
Ack! So close!

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.890
Definitely not! Don't forget 
about your hip injury!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:49.650
We got this far after switching to this 
pitching style so it can heal properly.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:54.430
If you pitch in a way that puts strain on 
your hip, we'll be back to square one.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:17:00.740
You may be tall, but the muscles holding
your body up are still that of a kid.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.710
Think about your future baseball career.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.260
<i>His timing's getting better.</i>

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:09.200
<i>If I get the location wrong, he'll hit it.</i>

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:12.570
Ball!

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:18.300
Ball!

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.220
Ball! Ball four!

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.530
All right! Bases loaded!

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:29.020
Now, it's between him and Satou!

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.770
Good luck, Hikaru-kun!

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:34.780
Batting fourth, center fielder, Satou-kun.

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:38.430
Ball!

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:40.450
Ball!

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:44.410
Three balls. No strikes!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.810
He might force in the runner here!

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.330
Stay sharp!

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:52.900
Tamaki!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.610
Only for this inning!

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:57.800
I'm only allowing you to do it this inning!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.470
Crush this cleanup!

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.710
<i>"Allowing"?</i>

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.770
<i>What does he mean by that?</i>

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:08.240
<i>Don't tell me he has 
something else up his sleeve.</i>

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.340
<i>Thank you... Manager...</i>

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:15.090
<i>If I can use this...</i>

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:20.450
<i>I will definitely win this game!</i>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.690
Strike!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.290
You've gotta be kidding me...

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:35.300
Are you telling me he's had a pitch 
like that in reserve all this time?!

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.890
<i>Why has he waited till 
now to throw that pitch?</i>

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.160
<i>Tamaki's max speed is
115 kilometers per hour.</i>

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:47.650
<i>The only grade schoolers who can 
hit it are Touto Boys' players.</i>

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:50.800
<i>If I think about the future,</i>

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:54.020
<i>I can understand the need to hold back now.</i>

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:59.360
<i>I don't like being underhanded, but in order 
to win, I'll do whatever it takes.</i>

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:05.580
<i>But all this time, I've wanted to steamroll
our opponents with my true strength!</i>

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:10.830
<i>That's what I'll do to
this batter, and then...</i>

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.390
No way...

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:28.680
It's outta here!

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:32.020
We've taken the lead with a grand slam!

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:34.650
<i>Is this guy for real?</i>

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.570
Amazing! That was amazing, Hikaru!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:40.080
You're a baseball genius!

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.860
Oh, come on, don't exaggerate.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.190
No, I mean it.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:47.920
It's just that, in Gunma,

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:52.680
the only way I could practice was 
to hit fastballs at the batting center.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:20:00.030
Maybe I timed that fastball because it was 
randomly like the ones I'm used to hitting.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:04.550
Don't worry about it. 
That was just a bad match-up.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:08.780
Chin up. It's not over yet.

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:10.900
Yes, sir.

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:19.070
Nijigaoka

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:19.070
Mifune

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.180
Strike! Batter out!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:41.800
Nijigaoka

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:41.800
Mifune

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:39.970
That's game.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:47.860
Bow!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.640
Thank you!

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.920
That was a nice game, Tashiro-kun.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.190
Thank you.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.360
No, the honor was all ours.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.840
Thank you very much.

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:02.140
Good luck in your next game.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.990
Um, Mr. Manager?

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.120
What is it?

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:11.740
How come your pitcher didn't pitch 
seriously until the very end?

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:16.200
He wasn't holding back, 
if that's what you're thinking.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:18.880
It's just...

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.300
Manager, let me tell them.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:25.680
I've got a hip injury.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:30.560
Coach and I decided on that pitching style 
so I don't put unnecessary strain on it

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.700
until it's fully healed.

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:36.400
Since I can't pitch at full speed,

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.770
I've done whatever it takes to win.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:41.960
Sorry about earlier.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:42.690
Huh?

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:44.820
No, that was...

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:49.720
However, that self-imposed 
ban was lifted in the sixth.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:53.870
Since that ball was hit all the way 
to the stands, I've got no regrets.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:56.400
Right.

00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:00.160
Wait!

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:05.800
When your injury's healed up,
 let's play again for real!

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:08.060
Sure.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:10.760
I definitely won't lose a rematch.

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:12.560
Neither will we.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:13.900
It's a promise, then!

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:25.130
<i>Let's play each other again someday!</i>

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:04.090
In the third-round match, Nagai 
replaces Sakura in the starting lineup.

00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:06.420
He's really fired up!

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:08.170
I can't lag behind, either!

00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:13.560
Let's do this, Hikaru! Let's win this one,
 too, and advance to the quarterfinals!

00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:17.070
Then, we'll finally get to 
see the monstrous team

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:20.300
known as the Touto Boys, 
that Urabe wants to beat.

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
I Don't Want to Lose

00:24:20.740 --> 00:24:22.900
Next time: "I Don't Want to Lose"!

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:25.020
Run to the stage of your dreams!
